       /proc/pid/statm - memory usage information

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_t_a_t_m
              Provides information about memory usage, measured in pages.  The
              columns are:

                  size       (1) total program size
                             (same as VmSize in _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_t_a_t_u_s)
                  resident   (2) resident set size
                             (inaccurate; same as VmRSS in _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_t_a_t_u_s)
                  shared     (3) number of resident shared pages
                             (i.e., backed by a file)
                             (inaccurate; same as RssFile+RssShmem in
                             _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_t_a_t_u_s)
                  text       (4) text (code)
                  lib        (5) library (unused since Linux 2.6; always 0)
                  data       (6) data + stack
                  dt         (7) dirty pages (unused since Linux 2.6; always 0)

              Some of these values are inaccurate because of a kernel‐internal
              scalability  optimization.  If accurate values are required, use
              _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_m_a_p_s or  _/_p_r_o_c_/pid_/_s_m_a_p_s___r_o_l_l_u_p  instead,  which  are
              much slower but provide accurate, detailed information.

